    "body": "# [kimik3][ROCm][Perf]Fuse the MLA q/kv RMSNorm pair in the module forward\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nMerge the MLA layer's two RMSNorms — `q_a_layernorm` (q_lora_rank) and\r\n`kv_a_layernorm` (kv_lora_rank) — into a single AITER `fused_qk_rmsnorm` launch,\r\nemitted from `MultiHeadLatentAttentionWrapper.forward` when AITER is enabled and a\r\nq latent exists.\r\n\r\nGuarded by `torch.compiler.is_compiling()` so compiled models keep using\r\n`MLADualRMSNormFusionPass`. Both paths emit the same\r\n`torch.ops.vllm.fused_mla_dual_rms_norm` op, so this changes only where it is\r\nchosen, not the kernel or its semantics.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\nKimi-K3 MXFP4, MI355X TP8, DSpark MTP, ISL 128k / OSL 1k, conc 8, decode-phase\r\ntorch trace. K3 is the motivating case: it builds its MLA through\r\n`MultiHeadLatentAttentionWrapper` but is not compiled.\r\n\r\nRank 0 shows `aiter::fused_qk_rmsnorm_kernel<bf16,256,8,true,1>` **144×** = 24 MLA\r\nlayers x 6 profiled engine steps, with the paired per-MLA-layer `add_rmsnorm_quant`\r\nlaunches gone. Remaining `add_rmsnorm_quant` counts are the unrelated per-layer\r\ninput/post-attention norms across all 93 layers.\r\n\r\nCompiled MLA models are unaffected by construction, and non-AITER builds never\r\nenter the branch.\r\n",
